WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.753
Welcome to Nabulines Academy.

2
00:00:02.009 --> 00:00:03.483
Today we're talking about money.

3
00:00:03.773 --> 00:00:05.492
What does it actually cost to build?

4
00:00:05.782 --> 00:00:06.931
Can you start for free?

5
00:00:07.117 --> 00:00:08.150
When do you need to pay?

6
00:00:08.406 --> 00:00:09.822
And how do you pay if you don't have a

7
00:00:09.857 --> 00:00:10.461
credit card?

8
00:00:11.006 --> 00:00:12.202
We're going to answer all of that,

9
00:00:12.225 --> 00:00:13.862
honestly, with real numbers.

10
00:00:13.920 --> 00:00:14.675
Let's go.

11
00:00:14.675 --> 00:00:16.834
First, the best news: you can start

12
00:00:16.893 --> 00:00:18.669
building and even deploy real sites for

13
00:00:18.727 --> 00:00:19.528
zero dollars.

14
00:00:20.271 --> 00:00:21.978
Here's the completely free path.

15
00:00:22.616 --> 00:00:24.509
Claude dot AI has a free plan.

16
00:00:25.054 --> 00:00:27.655
It gives you chat plus Artifacts — that's

17
00:00:27.701 --> 00:00:29.304
the live preview window where you build

18
00:00:29.362 --> 00:00:30.859
pages right in your browser.

19
00:00:31.498 --> 00:00:33.762
It's limited daily usage, but it's enough

20
00:00:33.808 --> 00:00:35.492
to learn and build your first apps.

21
00:00:36.130 --> 00:00:37.048
GitHub is free.

22
00:00:37.454 --> 00:00:39.056
Unlimited public repositories.

23
00:00:39.346 --> 00:00:40.937
You can store all your code there without

24
00:00:40.972 --> 00:00:41.750
paying anything.

25
00:00:42.214 --> 00:00:43.608
Cloudflare Pages is free.

26
00:00:43.898 --> 00:00:45.755
You can deploy a real website on a pages

27
00:00:45.813 --> 00:00:48.379
dot dev URL, live on the internet, for

28
00:00:48.437 --> 00:00:49.273
zero dollars.

29
00:00:49.622 --> 00:00:51.270
So Chapters zero through three of this

30
00:00:51.340 --> 00:00:53.836
course — your first sites, your first apps

31
00:00:53.975 --> 00:00:55.845
— you can do all of that without spending

32
00:00:55.879 --> 00:00:56.367
a cent.

33
00:00:56.622 --> 00:00:57.482
That's the promise.

34
00:00:57.667 --> 00:00:59.165
You don't need money to start.

35
00:00:59.165 --> 00:01:00.837
Now, when do costs appear?

36
00:01:01.127 --> 00:01:02.996
They show up when you want more power or

37
00:01:03.054 --> 00:01:03.739
more tools.

38
00:01:04.285 --> 00:01:06.375
Claude Code is the command-line tool that

39
00:01:06.421 --> 00:01:07.907
writes and edits files for you.

40
00:01:08.314 --> 00:01:09.985
It's free to install, but to run it you

41
00:01:10.044 --> 00:01:12.377
need either a paid Claude plan or API

42
00:01:12.435 --> 00:01:12.934
credits.

43
00:01:13.573 --> 00:01:15.581
The entry point is Claude Pro at twenty

44
00:01:15.628 --> 00:01:16.417
dollars a month.

45
00:01:16.823 --> 00:01:18.519
That's the plan most learners start with

46
00:01:18.565 --> 00:01:20.225
when they're ready for Claude Code.

47
00:01:20.771 --> 00:01:23.035
If you use it heavily, there's Max five-x

48
00:01:23.093 --> 00:01:25.449
at a hundred a month, or Max twenty-x at

49
00:01:25.496 --> 00:01:26.378
two hundred a month.

50
00:01:26.924 --> 00:01:29.490
Those are as of this recording — always

51
00:01:29.536 --> 00:01:30.976
check the live pricing page.

52
00:01:31.382 --> 00:01:32.949
If you don't want a monthly subscription,

53
00:01:33.054 --> 00:01:35.248
you can use the Anthropic API instead.

54
00:01:35.597 --> 00:01:36.676
That's pay-as-you-go.

55
00:01:36.967 --> 00:01:38.812
You add credits and pay per token.

56
00:01:39.451 --> 00:01:41.494
Haiku four point five is one dollar per

57
00:01:41.552 --> 00:01:43.921
million input tokens, five dollars output.

58
00:01:44.385 --> 00:01:46.185
Sonnet four point six is three dollars

59
00:01:46.243 --> 00:01:47.671
input, fifteen output.

60
00:01:48.309 --> 00:01:50.132
Opus four point eight is five input,

61
00:01:50.202 --> 00:01:51.130
twenty-five output.

62
00:01:52.001 --> 00:01:53.964
There's no permanent free tier, but if

63
00:01:53.998 --> 00:01:55.194
you're only using Claude Code

64
00:01:55.217 --> 00:01:57.748
occasionally, API credits can be cheaper

65
00:01:57.795 --> 00:01:58.793
than a monthly plan.

66
00:01:59.664 --> 00:02:02.253
Prompt caching cuts cached input by about

67
00:02:02.323 --> 00:02:04.482
ninety percent, and batch requests are

68
00:02:04.517 --> 00:02:05.899
about fifty percent cheaper.

69
00:02:06.642 --> 00:02:09.335
So the API is a real option for light use.

70
00:02:09.335 --> 00:02:11.065
What if you don't have a credit card?

71
00:02:11.703 --> 00:02:13.979
This is common outside the US, and there

72
00:02:14.014 --> 00:02:15.198
are real solutions.

73
00:02:15.744 --> 00:02:17.752
OpenRouter is a service that gives you one

74
00:02:17.799 --> 00:02:20.399
API key for many models, including Claude.

75
00:02:20.864 --> 00:02:22.988
You pay as you go, and you can top up with

76
00:02:23.034 --> 00:02:25.391
crypto — specifically USDC.

77
00:02:25.937 --> 00:02:26.831
No card needed.

78
00:02:27.086 --> 00:02:28.596
It's the best option for learners who

79
00:02:28.654 --> 00:02:31.045
can't use a card but want full AI access.

80
00:02:31.591 --> 00:02:33.147
If you need a card for something like

81
00:02:33.402 --> 00:02:36.049
ElevenLabs or a Claude subscription, you

82
00:02:36.107 --> 00:02:37.942
can get a crypto-funded virtual card.

83
00:02:38.580 --> 00:02:40.693
These are Visa or Mastercard cards you

84
00:02:40.752 --> 00:02:42.818
load with cryptocurrency, then use

85
00:02:42.865 --> 00:02:44.316
anywhere cards are accepted.

86
00:02:44.954 --> 00:02:47.172
Services like this exist in most regions.

87
00:02:47.636 --> 00:02:50.307
So the no-card path is: OpenRouter plus

88
00:02:50.365 --> 00:02:52.303
crypto for your AI usage, and a

89
00:02:52.350 --> 00:02:54.207
crypto-funded virtual card for anything

90
00:02:54.265 --> 00:02:55.589
else that requires a card.

91
00:02:55.937 --> 00:02:56.750
It works.

92
00:02:56.750 --> 00:02:58.457
Let's talk about the other costs.

93
00:02:58.805 --> 00:03:00.918
A custom domain is about ten to twelve

94
00:03:00.941 --> 00:03:01.731
dollars a year.

95
00:03:02.137 --> 00:03:04.366
You don't need one to start — Cloudflare

96
00:03:04.401 --> 00:03:07.698
gives you a free pages dot dev URL — but

97
00:03:07.733 --> 00:03:09.904
when you're ready for a real domain, it's

98
00:03:09.962 --> 00:03:10.368
cheap.

99
00:03:10.914 --> 00:03:12.888
Infrastructure: GitHub is free.

100
00:03:13.631 --> 00:03:14.977
Cloudflare Pages is free.

101
00:03:15.616 --> 00:03:18.275
Cloudflare R2 for storing video or files

102
00:03:18.530 --> 00:03:20.481
is about one and a half cents per gigabyte

103
00:03:20.515 --> 00:03:22.176
stored, with free egress.

104
00:03:22.814 --> 00:03:24.672
For this course, that's under a dollar a

105
00:03:24.730 --> 00:03:25.125
month.

106
00:03:25.868 --> 00:03:29.107
A VPS — a virtual private server, a Linux

107
00:03:29.165 --> 00:03:31.487
box in the cloud — costs about five to

108
00:03:31.545 --> 00:03:33.136
fifteen dollars a month depending on the

109
00:03:33.171 --> 00:03:33.739
provider.

110
00:03:34.378 --> 00:03:36.352
You'll need one later for always-on agents

111
00:03:36.410 --> 00:03:38.360
or automation, but not at the start.

112
00:03:39.103 --> 00:03:41.007
ElevenLabs is only needed if you're doing

113
00:03:41.042 --> 00:03:42.922
the automation and creator track —

114
00:03:43.561 --> 00:03:45.964
generating narration for videos or apps.

115
00:03:46.429 --> 00:03:48.170
The free plan gives you about ten minutes

116
00:03:48.205 --> 00:03:49.145
of audio a month.

117
00:03:49.784 --> 00:03:51.584
Starter is five dollars a month for about

118
00:03:51.630 --> 00:03:52.385
thirty minutes.

119
00:03:52.930 --> 00:03:54.985
Creator is twenty-two dollars for about a

120
00:03:55.055 --> 00:03:55.902
hundred minutes.

121
00:03:56.541 --> 00:03:58.677
Pro is ninety-nine dollars for about five

122
00:03:58.712 --> 00:03:59.432
hundred minutes.

123
00:04:00.175 --> 00:04:02.032
These prices are as of this recording —

124
00:04:02.137 --> 00:04:03.100
check their live page.

125
00:04:03.739 --> 00:04:06.235
ElevenLabs only accepts cards, so if you

126
00:04:06.258 --> 00:04:08.127
don't have one, you'd use a crypto-funded

127
00:04:08.174 --> 00:04:09.103
virtual card.

128
00:04:09.103 --> 00:04:10.844
So what's the honest monthly picture?

129
00:04:11.135 --> 00:04:12.632
If you're just learning and staying in the

130
00:04:12.656 --> 00:04:15.210
browser, Chapters zero through three, it's

131
00:04:15.280 --> 00:04:16.104
zero dollars.

132
00:04:16.975 --> 00:04:18.821
If you're serious and want Claude Code,

133
00:04:19.111 --> 00:04:20.504
you're looking at about twenty dollars a

134
00:04:20.550 --> 00:04:22.675
month for Claude Pro, plus maybe a dollar

135
00:04:22.721 --> 00:04:24.149
a year for a domain if you split it

136
00:04:24.196 --> 00:04:24.695
monthly.

137
00:04:25.333 --> 00:04:26.425
That's the builder path.

138
00:04:26.715 --> 00:04:28.503
If you're going full creator — your own

139
00:04:28.549 --> 00:04:30.964
tools, narration, always-on agents —

140
00:04:31.220 --> 00:04:32.694
you're looking at about twenty dollars for

141
00:04:32.740 --> 00:04:35.004
Claude Pro, five to twenty-two dollars for

142
00:04:35.062 --> 00:04:37.315
ElevenLabs depending on how much audio you

143
00:04:37.373 --> 00:04:39.312
generate, five to fifteen dollars for a

144
00:04:39.358 --> 00:04:42.133
VPS, and under a dollar for R2 storage.

145
00:04:42.771 --> 00:04:44.896
Total: about thirty to sixty dollars a

146
00:04:44.943 --> 00:04:45.291
month.

147
00:04:45.697 --> 00:04:46.707
That's the full stack.

148
00:04:47.450 --> 00:04:49.389
But remember: you start at zero.

149
00:04:49.679 --> 00:04:50.283
You build.

150
00:04:50.422 --> 00:04:51.014
You learn.

151
00:04:51.560 --> 00:04:52.965
You only pay when you're ready for more

152
00:04:52.999 --> 00:04:53.487
power.

153
00:04:54.033 --> 00:04:56.192
No one's asking you for money on day one.

154
00:04:56.192 --> 00:04:56.958
One more thing.

155
00:04:57.249 --> 00:04:58.235
Prices change.

156
00:04:58.874 --> 00:05:00.650
The numbers I just gave you are current as

157
00:05:00.708 --> 00:05:02.833
of this recording, but tools update their

158
00:05:02.879 --> 00:05:03.355
pricing.

159
00:05:03.994 --> 00:05:06.211
Always check the live page before you pay.

160
00:05:06.850 --> 00:05:08.789
The lesson here isn't the exact dollar

161
00:05:08.835 --> 00:05:10.681
amount — it's that you know what to

162
00:05:10.739 --> 00:05:13.525
expect, you know the free path exists, and

163
00:05:13.583 --> 00:05:15.232
you know how to pay even without a card.

164
00:05:15.870 --> 00:05:17.693
That's the honesty you need to plan.

165
00:05:17.693 --> 00:05:19.075
That's the honest breakdown.

166
00:05:19.330 --> 00:05:20.514
You can start for free.

167
00:05:20.700 --> 00:05:21.791
You pay when you're ready.

168
00:05:22.082 --> 00:05:24.009
And there are real solutions if you don't

169
00:05:24.044 --> 00:05:24.903
have a credit card.

170
00:05:25.448 --> 00:05:27.585
Your exercise: write down your monthly

171
00:05:27.643 --> 00:05:28.548
budget for tools.

172
00:05:28.955 --> 00:05:31.532
Even if it's zero to start, write it down.

173
00:05:32.077 --> 00:05:33.865
Know what you can afford, and plan your

174
00:05:33.900 --> 00:05:34.295
path.

175
00:05:35.305 --> 00:05:37.639
Next lesson, we're installing Claude Code.

176
00:05:38.509 --> 00:05:40.193
That's where the real building begins.

177
00:05:40.831 --> 00:05:41.702
See you there.
